==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_LeastPrivilegeStructural  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_LeastPrivilegeStructural.als
    rationale: Removing the role/op permission constraint and forcing a Doctor to succeed at the admin-only ListAudit endpoint produces an instance where a Permitted operation falls outside PermMatrix.Allowed — exactly what LeastPrivilege rules out.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompletenessFact  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AuditCompletenessFact.als
    rationale: Clearing the audit-completeness fact and inserting an authenticated RecordLookup that has no audit entry breaks the one-audit-per-clinical-access invariant.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_012_AuditPerAccess, FR_015_NoPermittedWithoutAudit
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_AuditPerAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_NoPermittedWithoutAudit: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_CareTeamGating  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_CareTeamGating.als
    rationale: Without care-team gating, a Permitted RecordLookup can exist for a caller with no membership row — directly violating the ownership-based access invariant.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_004_CareTeamGating
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_004_CareTeamGating: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditSnapshotsMatchOp  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AuditSnapshotsMatchOp.als
    rationale: Without the snapshot-equality fact, an AuditEntry can record a different user than the operation's actual caller — a textbook misattribution counterexample.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_013_AuditSnapshot
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_AuditSnapshot: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ExternalResponseShape  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_ExternalResponseShape.als
    rationale: Clearing the response-shape fact and forcing two non-Permitted operations to differ in externalResponse reveals the existence/non-existence distinction that FR-006 forbids.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_006_ByteEquivalentNotFound
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_006_ByteEquivalentNotFound: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NoteUniqueCreatingOp  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_NoteUniqueCreatingOp.als
    rationale: Without the unique-creator constraint, two distinct operations can share a ClinicalNote — the cleanest static stand-in for note mutation/duplication that append-only rules out.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_011_NotesAppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_011_NotesAppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

